{
  "abstract": "Let f(n) be the sum over prime divisors p of n of the greatest power of p at most n. The weighted sum of f(n)/n over 1 ≤ n < x is asymptotic to an explicit sum over primes p ≤ (log x)^2. Each prime contributes a term depending on the remainder of log x modulo log p. The proof combines a finite harmonic-sum estimate with a uniform short-interval prime bound.",
  "authors": [
